{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1810,1958p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go\"","aggregated_output":"\tif expectedContext != \"\" {\n\t\tguard = func() error {\n\t\t\tlatest, err := posemodel.ResolveAgentProjectContext(resolver, currentProject, taskRef)\n\t\t\tif err != nil || latest.ContextRevision != expectedContext || latest.Authority == nil || latest.Authority.String() != context.Authority.String() {\n\t\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"stale-context\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn cmdCloseLocalWithStoreEffect(store, localRef, guard, stdout, stderr, nil)\n}\n\nfunc scopeRefForArtifact(ref posemodel.ArtifactRef) string {\n\tif ref.Kind == \"milestone\" {\n\t\treturn \"milestone:\" + ref.Slug + \"/\" + ref.Milestone\n\t}\n\treturn ref.Kind + \":\" + ref.Slug\n}\n\nfunc cmdCloseLocal(root, ref string, guard func() error, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n\treturn cmdCloseLocalWithEffect(root, ref, guard, stdout, stderr, nil)\n}\n\n// The pipeline confirms a transition only from the write point, never exit 0\n// alone: another execution may have closed the scope since it planned.\nfunc cmdCloseLocalWithEffect(root, ref string, guard func() error, stdout, stderr io.Writer, transitioned func(unsynced error)) int {\n\treturn cmdCloseLocalWithStoreEffect(cliGovernedStore(root), ref, guard, stdout, stderr, transitioned)\n}\n\nfunc cmdCloseLocalWithStoreEffect(store posemodel.Store, ref string, guard func() error, stdout, stderr io.Writer, transitioned func(unsynced error)) int {\n\tif scope, parseErr := posemodel.ParseScopeRef(ref); parseErr == nil && scope.Kind == \"spec\" {\n\t\tstate, err := cliCloseoutStateForStore(store, ref)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tif refusal := cliCloseGovernedPreflightRefusal(store, ref); refusal != nil {\n\t\t\t\terr = refusal\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose close: \" + err.Error())\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tif state.LifecycleDone {\n\t\t\tif !state.Terminal {\n\t\t\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose close: terminal verification blocked: \" + strings.Join(state.Blockers, \"; \") + \"; \" + state.NextAction)\n\t\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Field(\"close.already-satisfied\", ref+\"; applicable terminal verifier passed; no transition executed\")\n\t\t\treturn 0\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar result int\n\terr := store.WithCloseoutWriteGuard(\"close.transition\", ref, func(guarded posemodel.Store) error {\n\t\tresult = cmdCloseLocalWithGuardedStore(guarded.Root, guarded, ref, guard, stdout, stderr, transitioned)\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif refusal := cliCloseGovernedPreflightRefusal(store, ref); refusal != nil {\n\t\t\terr = refusal\n\t\t}\n\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose close: \" + err.Error())\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn result\n}\n\n// A disabled review bundle policy must not hide an adopted action restriction\n// when closeout preflight fails. This local lease permits only a\n// refusal: it never substitutes for full root discovery, the guarded closeout\n// evaluation, lifecycle lock or CAS required for a successful transition.\nfunc cliCloseGovernedPreflightRefusal(store posemodel.Store, ref string) error {\n\tscope, err := posemodel.ParseScopeRef(ref)\n\tif err != nil || scope.Kind != \"spec\" {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\treturn store.WithGovernanceWriteGuardForProjects(\"close.restriction-refusal\", nil, func(guarded posemodel.Store) error {\n\t\tpolicy, err := guarded.GetReviewPolicy()\n\t\tif err != nil || policy.Enabled || policy.AgencyReadinessVersion != posemodel.AgencyReadinessPolicyVersion {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\trestrictions, err := guarded.GovernedEffectRestrictions(posemodel.PhaseCloseout, []string{scope.Slug})\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tmessages := make([]string, 0, len(restrictions))\n\t\tfor _, restriction := range restrictions {\n\t\t\tmessages = append(messages, fmt.Sprintf(\"%s restricts closeout: %s\", restriction.Source.Detail, restriction.Message))\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(messages) > 0 {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"action-request-pending: %s\", strings.Join(messages, \"; \"))\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n}\n\nfunc cmdCloseLocalWithGuardedStore(root string, store posemodel.Store, ref string, guard func() error, stdout, stderr io.Writer, transitioned func(unsynced error)) int {\n\t// The gates below judge the artifact as it is now; the transition is\n\t// published only over those same bytes (spec\n\t// pose-writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication R4).\n\tjudged := closeTargetDigest(root, store, ref)\n\tstate, err := cliCloseoutStateForStore(store, ref)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, \"pose close: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\t// Repeating close on an already-done spec is a readonly terminal check,\n\t// bounded by the same historical contract as closeout-check and the plan.\n\tif scope, parseErr := posemodel.ParseScopeRef(ref); parseErr == nil && scope.Kind == \"spec\" && state.LifecycleDone {\n\t\tif !state.Terminal {\n\t\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(\"pose close: terminal verification blocked: \" + strings.Join(state.Blockers, \"; \") + \"; \" + state.NextAction)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\trender(stdout, stderr).Field(\"close.already-satisfied\", ref+\"; applicable terminal verifier passed; no transition executed\")\n\t\treturn 0\n\t}\n\t// Governed effects (spec pose-governed-effect-enforcement): this is the\n\t// write point of the closeout transition, so an adopted, unsatisfied\n\t// action request restricting closeout refuses here with its typed cause,\n\t// whatever else the scope's review says.\n\tgoverned := []string{}\n\tfor _, d := range state.Diagnostics {\n\t\tif d.Code == \"action-request-pending\" {\n\t\t\tgoverned = append(governed, d.Message)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\t// A current adjudication that says a question does not hold refuses the\n\t// closeout (spec pose-delegated-verdict-destinations R1).\n\tadjudicated := []string{}\n\tfor _, d := range state.Diagnostics {\n\t\tif d.Code == posemodel.AdjudicationDoesNotHoldCode {\n\t\t\tadjudicated = append(adjudicated, d.Message)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(adjudicated) > 0 {\n\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n\t\tfor _, message := range adjudicated {\n\t\t\tout.Field(\"close.refused.adjudication\", message)\n\t\t}\n\t\tout.Failure(fmt.Sprintf(\"pose close: %d adjudicated question(s) of %s do not hold\", len(adjudicated), ref))\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tif len(governed) > 0 {\n\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n\t\tfor _, message := range governed {\n\t\t\tout.Field(\"close.refused.action-request-pending\", message)\n\t\t}\n\t\tout.Failure(fmt.Sprintf(\"pose close: %d action request(s) restrict closeout of %s\", len(governed), ref))\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\tscope, _ := posemodel.ParseScopeRef(ref)\n\t// Under an adopted closeout review policy (spec\n\t// pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit) the close of a milestone or a\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining issues are in review projections: an aggregate’s own approval can report `closed` before explicit close; an exemption can discard child-review blockers; and review planning still reads a transferred member’s source stub.\n\nThe temporary overlay probe could not run because the sandbox has no writable temporary directory. I’ll distinguish those code-based findings from the passing regression tests in the conclusion. The repository is unchanged.\n"}}
